    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0359" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 713.001/71</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-14T10:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 14, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Central American Court of Justice had formal closing session at 3 p.m., 12th
                    instant; archives and property turned over to the Costa Rican Government.
                    Closing resolution included one to call upon Tinoco and amicably request full
                    amnesty be given all political prisoners. Undoubtedly political move dictated by
                    almost unanimous hostility of members towards him. Call made, but military
                    process against prisoners continues and further arrests made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
